            <ArticleTitle>Arthrocentesis: the latest on joint pain relief.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>34-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/01.NPR.0000431180.87429.03</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Arthrocentesis is a procedure in the diagnostic workup and treatment of joint pain that has few complications. Analysis of joint fluid yields important treatment data. Corticosteroid and local anesthetic injections provide longer pain relief.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
